# Project operating model

Principle: **production-grade thinking, educational-grade process**.

Default flow:

`task classification → candidate/readiness analysis → mini use case when
required → source/architecture/planning gates → PRE_PLAN_READINESS verdict →
concise technical plan → one implementation tranche → focused tests → one
review → HANDOFF update → one coherent commit`

## Task levels

1. **Quick technical task or spike**
   analysis → implementation → test → review → commit.
   Behaviour-changing quick work still requires `PRE_PLAN_READINESS: READY`
   (or reclassify as a normal feature). Pure technical work may use
   `NO_USE_CASE_CHANGE`.

2. **Normal feature**
   mini use case → plan → implementation → tests → review → handoff → commit.

3. **Major architectural decision**
   PM/BA analysis → use case → ADR when required → plan → implementation →
   review → commit.

ADR is required only for a new module, aggregate, public API, database schema,
Kafka topic, security-boundary change, or another costly-to-reverse decision.

## PRE_PLAN_READINESS principles

- Technical-only tasks may return `NO_USE_CASE_CHANGE` (or
  `QUALITY_SCENARIO_ONLY` / `ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_ONLY`).
- Behaviour-changing work must pass `PRE_PLAN_READINESS`.
- Technical planning for business work starts only when the verdict is `READY`.
- Blocked work updates `HANDOFF.md` with the exact missing source, decision,
  capability or executable verification.
- Product Manager is used only for a new epic or unclear value/direction.

The structured contract lives in `.cursor/rules/10-use-case-and-feature-planning.mdc`
and is assembled by existing skills — do not duplicate the checklist here.

## What ordinary local work must not depend on

Do **not** block safe local educational implementation on:

- review councils;
- owner decision packets;
- approval queues;
- implementation admission records;
- canonical migration admission;
- repeated closure audits;
- production legal/regulatory closure;
- multiple documentation-only commits.

Unresolved production topics are recorded as `BLOCKED_FOR_PRODUCTION`.
They must not block safe local educational implementation.

## Role routing (not all roles every time)

| Task kind | Roles |
|---|---|
| Quick technical task | Technical Architect + Scrum Master |
| Normal feature | Business Analyst + `enterprise-use-case-engineering` + Technical Architect + Scrum Master |
| New epic / unclear direction | Product Manager + Business Analyst + `enterprise-use-case-engineering` + Technical Architect + Scrum Master |
| Technical spike | Technical Architect + Scrum Master |

Role skills live under `.claude/skills/{product-manager,business-analyst,technical-architect,scrum-master}/`.

## Validation policy

Focused validation only:

- use-case change → use-case/traceability validator;
- database change → migration, Testcontainers and RLS tests;
- backend change → relevant module and integration tests;
- UI change → typecheck, component tests and at most the relevant smoke;
- every commit → focused tests plus `git diff --check`.

Full governance validation is reserved for epic closure, milestone, major merge,
or production-readiness work.

## Safety and authority

- Read `HANDOFF.md` before material work.
- Preserve ADR-N1…N17 and `[FREEZE]` decisions; do not invent rail or regulatory facts.
- Do not fabricate human approval.
- Do not push or run destructive Git operations unless the user explicitly authorises them.
- Prefer one coherent commit after review; do not create documentation-only commit chains for process theatre.
- Phase E review/planning paths use `.cursor/rules/10-phase-e-governance.mdc` only when those paths are touched; that rule does not govern ordinary implementation.
